Interview title: {{ title }}

Persona: {{ persona }}

{%- if variant_strategy == "all_angles" %}
Total LOGICAL questions to produce: {{ question_count }}.
For EACH logical question, write exactly {{ angles|length }} variants — one of each
type in [{{ angles|join(', ') }}]. Give all four rows the SAME integer
``logical_question_index`` (starting at 0), the SAME concrete underlying problem,
the SAME linked_outcome_id, and the SAME difficulty. The variants must be
meaningfully different probes of that one problem, NEVER paraphrases or four
independent questions: technical asks correctness / edge cases, system_design
asks architecture / trade-offs, situational poses a case study, behavioral asks
experience / approach. Total rows = {{ question_count * angles|length }}.

Difficulty is assigned per LOGICAL question (all its variants share the SAME
difficulty), ramping across the logical questions:
- logical questions 1-3: easy   (expected_depth 1-2)
- logical questions 4-7: medium (expected_depth 2-4)
- logical questions 8+ : hard   (expected_depth 3-5)
{%- elif variant_strategy == "role_only" %}
Total questions to produce: {{ question_count }}.
Every question MUST have question_type "{{ role_type }}".

Difficulty progression rubric:
- positions 1-3: easy   (expected_depth 1-2)
- positions 4-7: medium (expected_depth 2-4)
- positions 8+ : hard   (expected_depth 3-5)
{%- else %}
Total questions to produce: {{ question_count }}

Type mix (the produced set must match these proportions, rounded):
- technical: {{ technical_pct }}%
- behavioral: {{ behavioral_pct }}%
- situational: {{ situational_pct }}%

Difficulty progression rubric:
- positions 1-3: easy   (expected_depth 1-2)
- positions 4-7: medium (expected_depth 2-4)
- positions 8+ : hard   (expected_depth 3-5)
{%- endif %}
{%- if supplementary_instructions %}

Teacher's supplementary instructions:
{{ supplementary_instructions }}
{%- endif %}

Learning outcomes the interview must assess (link each question to one
outcome ID):
{%- if outcomes %}
{%- for outcome in outcomes %}
- id: {{ outcome.id }}
  type: {{ outcome.outcome_type }}
  weight: {{ outcome.importance_weight }}
  text: {{ outcome.outcome_text }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
(no outcomes provided — link_outcome_id MUST be null in the output)
{%- endif %}

{%- if avoid_prompts %}

Questions already accepted for this interview — do NOT repeat these or
produce close paraphrases of them:
{%- for prompt in avoid_prompts %}
- {{ prompt }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}

Source context (chunks the interview should be grounded in):
{{ chunks_block }}

Grounding rule: every question MUST cite at least one chunk from the
source-context block above in its "source_refs" (copy the chunk id exactly).
A question with an empty source_refs array will be REJECTED.

Return JSON in this shape:
{
  "questions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "logical_question_index": 0,
      "question_type": "technical",
      "prompt_text": "...",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "expected_depth": 2,
      "linked_outcome_id": "<one of the outcome ids above, or null>",
      "source_refs": ["<chunk uuid from the source-context block>"],
      "rationale": "...",
      "model_answer": "..."
    }
  ]
}
